{"1-12":{"people":[{"id":"festus-g5347","name":"Festus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":4,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":7,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":5,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"claudius-g2804g","name":"Claudius","kind":"person","brief":"Roman Emperor","count":4,"firstVerse":8}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":4,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"caesarea-g2542h","name":"Caesarea","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":1}],"words":[{"base":"G2541","lemma":"Καῖσαρ","tr":"Kaisar","gloss":"Caesar","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":29},{"base":"G3972","lemma":"Παῦλος","tr":"Paulos","gloss":"Paul","lang":"g","inPassage":6,"uses":158},{"base":"G5347","lemma":"Φῆστος","tr":"Phēstos","gloss":"Festus","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":13},{"base":"G2453","lemma":"Ἰουδαῖος","tr":"Ioudaios","gloss":"Jew","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":194},{"base":"G2542","lemma":"Καισάρεια","tr":"Kaisareia","gloss":"Caesarea","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":17},{"base":"G2414","lemma":"Ἱεροσόλυμα","tr":"Hierosoluma","gloss":"Jerusalem","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":62},{"base":"G3777","lemma":"οὔτε","tr":"oute","gloss":"neither","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":87},{"base":"G3767","lemma":"οὖν","tr":"oun","gloss":"therefore","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":497},{"base":"G0968","lemma":"βῆμα","tr":"bēma","gloss":"judgement seat","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"G1909","lemma":"ἐπί","tr":"epi","gloss":"upon","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":885}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":24,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Yet my accusers did not find me debating with anyone in the temple or riling up a crowd in the synagogues or in the city.","from":8},{"book":"ACT","chapter":24,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Nor can they prove to you any of their charges against me.","from":7},{"book":"ACT","chapter":28,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"After three days, he called together the leaders of the Jews. When they had gathered, he said to them, “Brothers, although I have done nothing against our people or the customs of our fathers, I was taken prisoner in Jerusalem and handed over to the Romans.","from":8},{"book":"ACT","chapter":28,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"But when the Jews objected, I was compelled to appeal to Caesar, even though I have no charge to bring against my nation.","from":11},{"book":"ACT","chapter":24,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"After two years had passed, Felix was succeeded by Porcius Festus. And wishing to do the Jews a favor, Felix left Paul in prison.","from":9},{"book":"ACT","chapter":25,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"While I was in Jerusalem, the chief priests and elders of the Jews presented their case and requested a judgment against him.","from":2},{"book":"ACT","chapter":25,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So when they came here with me, I did not delay. The next day I sat on the judgment seat and ordered that the man be brought in.","from":6},{"book":"ACT","chapter":26,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And Agrippa said to Festus, “This man could have been released if he had not appealed to Caesar.”","from":11}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":3},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":3},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2}]},"13-22":{"people":[{"id":"festus-g5347","name":"Festus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"agrippa-g0067","name":"Agrippa","kind":"person","brief":"A Tetrarch","count":2,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"bernice-g0959","name":"Bernice","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":3,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"felix-g5344","name":"Felix","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"augustus-g0828","name":"Augustus","kind":"person","brief":"Roman emperor","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"claudius-g2804g","name":"Claudius","kind":"person","brief":"Roman Emperor","count":1,"firstVerse":21}],"places":[{"id":"caesarea-g2542h","name":"Caesarea","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"rome-g4514","name":"Rome","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":16}],"words":[{"base":"G4012","lemma":"περί","tr":"peri","gloss":"about","lang":"g","inPassage":7,"uses":332},{"base":"G5347","lemma":"Φῆστος","tr":"Phēstos","gloss":"Festus","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":13},{"base":"G5100","lemma":"τις","tr":"tis","gloss":"one","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":530},{"base":"G2725","lemma":"κατήγορος","tr":"katēgoros","gloss":"accuser","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"G3972","lemma":"Παῦλος","tr":"Paulos","gloss":"Paul","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":158},{"base":"G4314","lemma":"πρός","tr":"pros","gloss":"to","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":700},{"base":"G0067","lemma":"Ἀγρίππας","tr":"Agrippas","gloss":"Agrippa","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"G2753","lemma":"κελεύω","tr":"keleuō","gloss":"to order","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":25},{"base":"G1014","lemma":"βούλομαι","tr":"boulomai","gloss":"to plan","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":37},{"base":"G2596","lemma":"κατά","tr":"kata","gloss":"according to","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":472}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JHN","chapter":7,"verse":51,"verseEnd":51,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"“Does our law convict a man without first hearing from him to determine what he has done?”","from":16},{"book":"ACT","chapter":23,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"I found that the accusation involved questions about their own law, but there was no charge worthy of death or imprisonment.","from":19},{"book":"ACT","chapter":24,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"After two years had passed, Felix was succeeded by Porcius Festus. And wishing to do the Jews a favor, Felix left Paul in prison.","from":14},{"book":"DEU","chapter":19,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"both parties to the dispute must stand in the presence of the LORD, before the priests and judges who are in office at that time.","from":16},{"book":"DEU","chapter":19,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"The judges shall investigate thoroughly, and if the witness is proven to be a liar who has falsely accused his brother,","from":16},{"book":"ACT","chapter":18,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But since it is a dispute about words and names and your own law, settle it yourselves. I refuse to be a judge of such things.”","from":19},{"book":"DEU","chapter":17,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and if it is reported and you hear about it, you must investigate it thoroughly. If the report is true and such an abomination has happened in Israel,","from":16},{"book":"DEU","chapter":19,"verse":17,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"both parties to the dispute must stand in the presence of the LORD, before the priests and judges who are in office at that time. The judges shall investigate thoroughly, and if the witness is proven to be a liar who has falsely accused his brother,","from":16}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":7},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":5},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":5},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":3},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2}]},"23-27":{"people":[{"id":"agrippa-g0067","name":"Agrippa","kind":"person","brief":"A Tetrarch","count":3,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"festus-g5347","name":"Festus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"bernice-g0959","name":"Bernice","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"augustus-g0828","name":"Augustus","kind":"person","brief":"Roman emperor","count":1,"firstVerse":25}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24}],"words":[{"base":"G0067","lemma":"Ἀγρίππας","tr":"Agrippas","gloss":"Agrippa","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":11},{"base":"G5347","lemma":"Φῆστος","tr":"Phēstos","gloss":"Festus","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":13},{"base":"G3992","lemma":"πέμπω","tr":"pempō","gloss":"to send","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":79},{"base":"G0935","lemma":"βασιλεύς","tr":"basileus","gloss":"king","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":115},{"base":"G1125","lemma":"γράφω","tr":"graphō","gloss":"to write","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":190},{"base":"G5037","lemma":"τε","tr":"te","gloss":"and","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":215},{"base":"G0435","lemma":"ἀνήρ","tr":"anēr","gloss":"man","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":216},{"base":"G4012","lemma":"περί","tr":"peri","gloss":"about","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":332},{"base":"G0249","lemma":"ἄλογος","tr":"alogos","gloss":"unreasonable","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G0959","lemma":"Βερνίκη","tr":"Bernikē","gloss":"Bernice","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":22,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The crowd listened to Paul until he made this statement. Then they lifted up their voices and shouted, “Rid the earth of him! He is not fit to live!”","from":24},{"book":"ACT","chapter":23,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"I found that the accusation involved questions about their own law, but there was no charge worthy of death or imprisonment.","from":25},{"book":"ACT","chapter":25,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"When Paul arrived, the Jews who had come down from Jerusalem stood around him, bringing many serious charges that they could not prove.","from":24},{"book":"EST","chapter":1,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And for a full 180 days he displayed the glorious riches of his kingdom and the magnificent splendor of his greatness.","from":23},{"book":"PRO","chapter":18,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"He who answers a matter before he hears it— this is folly and disgrace to him.","from":27},{"book":"ECC","chapter":1,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"“Futility of futilities,” says the Teacher, “futility of futilities! Everything is futile!”","from":23},{"book":"ISA","chapter":5,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Therefore Sheol enlarges its throat and opens wide its enormous jaws, and down go Zionʼs nobles and masses, her revelers and carousers!","from":23},{"book":"ISA","chapter":14,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Your pomp has been brought down to Sheol, along with the music of your harps. Maggots are your bed and worms your blanket.","from":23}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":4},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":3},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]}}